# Collision and Impulse Reference Manifest

This manifest supports Codex in calculating realistic collision effects, force dispersion, bounce behavior, and procedural destruction physics using verified mechanical principles.

---

##  Newtonian Impact Physics

**Name:** *Classical Mechanics  MIT OCW 8.01*  
**Type:** University Lecture Series  
**URL:** https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/physics/8-01sc-classical-mechanics-fall-2016/  

**Use:** Governs collision resolution, impulse momentum, and elastic vs inelastic bounce. Codex may simulate ragdoll knockback, ricochet logic, or shattered shields.

---

**Name:** *Impulse and Momentum  Physics Classroom*  
**Type:** Interactive Physics Resource  
**URL:** https://www.physicsclassroom.com/class/momentum  

**Use:** Tracks applied force over time for sudden impacts. Codex can generate believable hits, energy blade recoil, or slowed entropy hammer effects.

---

##  Fragmentation & Shatter Logic

**Name:** *Brittle Material Fracture Simulation  University of Illinois*  
**Type:** Materials Engineering Research  
**URL:** https://matse.illinois.edu/research/fracture-and-failure  

**Use:** Details crack propagation, fragment burst patterns. Codex may use this to model collapsing statues, crystal resonance implosions, or bone fractures.

---

**Name:** *Procedural Destruction  GDC Talk (Red Faction / Frostbite)*  
**Type:** Game Engine Engineering  
**URL:** https://www.gdcvault.com/play/1020061/Destruction-and-Physics-in-Red  

**Use:** Guidelines for runtime breakup of surfaces. Codex may use this to generate crumble thresholds, stress fractures, or reactive debris fields.

---

##  Bounce Curves & Object Recoil

**Name:** *Coefficient of Restitution  HyperPhysics*  
**Type:** Physics Portal  
**URL:** http://hyperphysics.phy-astr.gsu.edu/hbase/mechanics/coores.html  

**Use:** Defines how bouncy two objects behave after impact. Codex can model grenade ricochet, enemy bounce against shields, or fluid-object splashback.

---

**Name:** *Collision Detection & Response  Real-Time Collision Book (Christer Ericson)*  
**Type:** Game Physics Reference  
**URL:** https://www.crcpress.com/Real-Time-Collision-Detection/Ericson/p/book/9781558607323  

**Use:** Advanced collision accuracy and edge handling. Codex may simulate tight-hit surfaces, impact-solved motion, or boundary rebound zones.

---
